[
  {
    "sha": "40d5ffd638182937b5e3f1fc5976a706dd5da2a5",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDQwZDVmZmQ2MzgxODI5MzdiNWUzZjFmYzU5NzZhNzA2ZGQ1ZGEyYTU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-13T15:40:44Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-13T15:40:44Z"
      },
      "message": "ci(review): run the PR review's build on the self-hosted Linux runner\n\nAdds pr-test.yml (workflow_dispatch only: PR number + the head SHA the\nreviewer read; read-only token, no secrets, per-PR concurrency group,\nself-hosted linux runner). It checks out refs/pull/<N>/head, refuses any\nother head and any diff touching build.rs, .github/, scripts/, .cargo/,\na Cargo manifest or lock, or a toolchain file, trial-merges with main,\nruns `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (ui suites under\nxvfb-run) and clippy on the touched crates, and writes the gate summary\nto the run summary.\n\nThe PR-reviewer agent (step 2b) checks for an online runner and no cut\nin progress, dispatches the run after reading the diff, waits, and\nreads the per-binary result; otherwise it builds locally as before.\nCancelled, timed-out or unstarted runs are never a pass. review-prs and\nAGENTS.md say so. Decisions in docs/decisions/1420-pr-test-pipeline.md.\nPROCESS_VERSION 56 -> 57.\n\nFixes #1420\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
